{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Root cause (proven) — the defect is DIAGNOSTIC, not behavioral\n\n**Ticking an AC checkbox does NOT invalidate an attestation.** Confirmed empirically by\nrunning `pass1.material_fingerprint` over a tick-only description pair: the hashes are equal.\n`pass1._normalize_checkbox_state` rewrites `[x]`/`[X]` to `[ ]` before hashing (change 330c),\nand it applies to every basis key.\n\nThe material basis is a single composite sha256 over exactly `ticket_id`, `description`,\n`file_impact`, `children`, plus `file_impact_scope` when the scope is an explicit `none`.\n**\"AC\" is not a component at all** — acceptance criteria live inside `description`. Every\nstaleness message nonetheless recited `description/AC/file_impact/children`, naming an input\nthe fingerprint does not have and never saying which input actually differed.\n\nThat is what produced the three contradictory reports:\n\n- **846b (ticking was safe)** — correct, and now pinned by a test.\n- **c6c9 (ticking WITH evidence prose invalidated)** — correct: the added prose is a\n  `description` edit. The message could not say so.\n- **1909 (plain ticking invalidated)** — a real residual cause the message hid. A **pre-330c**\n  attestation hashed the RAW description. If it was signed while the boxes were already\n  ticked, later un-ticking one leaves neither the normalized recompute nor the\n  `attest._legacy_material_ok` grandfather (bug 96d1) able to match, so it reads\n  `stale-material` with nothing materially edited. (Signed while UNticked, it survives ticking\n  — the legacy basis is byte-identical to the normalized one.)\n\nDiscriminating experiment: the same composite was recomputed under both the normalized and the\nlegacy algorithm for tick-only, tick+prose, file_impact and children edits. Only the composite\ndistinguishes nothing; the per-component hashes distinguish all four.\n\n## Fix — Gerrit change 1434\n\nThe basis now hashes each key separately (`llm/plan_review/material_diff.py`), and the\nper-component fingerprints ride in the signed manifest as additive\n`material-part: <name> <hash16> <size>` lines and on the REVIEW_RESULT sidecar. Design chosen\nover replaying the event store to `signed_at`: `children` is derived from OTHER tickets'\n`parent_id` at read time, so a replay would need a whole-store rewind, and compaction squashes\nexactly the old events where legacy attestations live. The signed manifest is the only\ntrustworthy record of what the reviewer saw.\n\nBefore:\n\n    stale-material: the plan was materially edited since review\n    (description/AC/file_impact/children changed)\n\nAfter:\n\n    stale-material: the plan was materially edited since review —\n    changed: description (4210 -> 4396 chars), children (3 -> 4)\n\nSwept every attestation refusal surface, not just that one message: `stale-reopened` names both\ntimestamps; the claim gate's `unsigned` names both remedies; a relation-snapshot read failure at\nsigning time stops advising `sign-review` (which re-hits the same read) while every other abort\nkeeps it; `generation.py` names the changed dependency ids; `completion.py` forwards a child's\nclosure reason. `stale-code` and `stale-head` already named the drifted files and the two SHAs\nand are unchanged. Surfaces left alone because they already forward the reason verbatim:\n`_commands/gates.py`, `_commands/transition_close.py`, `llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py`.\n\n## No gate outcome changed\n\nEvery edit is inside the `reason` string of an already-failing branch or is an additive,\ndiagnostic-only manifest line. `manifest_material_parts` is deliberately lenient (a malformed\nline is skipped, not raised) so a cosmetic field can never convert a staleness refusal into a\nparse error. The composite fingerprint is byte-identical to before. Verified: a per-branch\n`(valid, verdict)` assertion for `unsigned` / `not-closed` / `stale-reopened` / `wrong-kind` /\n`stale-material`, plus `tests/unit` + `tests/integration` (8601 passed) and\n`tests/e2e`/`interfaces`/`lib` (1484 passed). The three unrelated failures\n(`test_coverage_reconstruction`, `test_jscpd_dup_heldout`, `test_identity_gate_scope_and_ledger`)\nreproduce on a pristine checkout of the same base commit — pre-existing tooling/environment\nfailures, not this change.\n"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785949470355666001,"uuid":"7c0c726a-ac58-42de-88a8-8d5fc5da172f"}